  "text_content": "Menu Student Files Classes Instructor Open submenu Reports Open submenu Set Class Schedule School Permits Close submenu Instructor Instructor Schedule Open submenu Instructor Reports Open submenu My Signatures Close submenu Instructor Schedule Booked Appointments Specify Hours Close submenu Instructor Reports Work Summary To Do Lists Close submenu Reports AQTR Registrations Ilan Preisler logout Self-Evaluation of In-Car Session Practical Session #5 Centeno, Arielle 1. In the Learner's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? S: W; thinking ahead, looking ahead, correct &#233;valuations, nervousness, 2. In the Instructor's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? Agree with student. Good basic control of car. To work on lifting eyes up and scanning further ahead, this will give you more time to analyze the situation and come up with a plan of action. Ensure mirrors are checked every 5-10 seconds. Avoid feeling that you have to kerp moving forward all the time.Try to practice more on multi-lane roadways and in denser traffic situations. Student Student Signature Centeno, Arielle Jan 26, 2026 Instructor Instructor Signature Tze L L12618 Save",
